---
import ComponentDoc from '../../layouts/ComponentDoc.astro';
import Section from '@esa/docs/Section.astro';
import Preview from '@esa/docs/Preview.astro';
import ApiTable from '@esa/docs/ApiTable.astro';
import LoadingOverlay from '@esa/ecology/esa-loading-overlay.astro';

// Prose only — names, types and defaults are generated from the component
// source by src/data/component-api.ts, so this table cannot drift.
const describe = {
  active: "When false the overlay renders nothing.",
  message: "Optional caption shown under the spinner.",
  transparent: "Semi-transparent backdrop instead of an opaque one.",
};
---
<ComponentDoc name="Loading Overlay" category="Display" slug="esa-loading-overlay" type=".astro" status="stable"
  summary="Covers its positioned parent with a centered spinner and optional message while a region is busy. Opaque or semi-transparent backdrop.">

  <Section id="preview" title="Preview">
    <p>Place the overlay inside a <code>position: relative</code> container; its absolute backdrop fills the parent.</p>
    <Preview align="start" code={`<div style="position: relative; min-height: 180px;">
  <p>Underlying content being covered.</p>
  <LoadingOverlay active={true} message="Loading data…" />
</div>`}>
      <div style="position: relative; min-height: 180px; width: 100%; border: 1px solid var(--color-border-default, #e5e5e5); border-radius: var(--radius-300, 0.5rem); padding: var(--spacing-400, 1rem);">
        <p style="margin: 0;">Underlying content that is being covered while loading.</p>
        <LoadingOverlay active={true} message="Loading data…" />
      </div>
    </Preview>
  </Section>

  <Section id="states" title="States">
    <p>A <code>transparent</code> backdrop lets the content show through faintly. When <code>active</code> is false the overlay renders nothing.</p>
    <Preview align="start" code={`<LoadingOverlay active={true} transparent={true} message="Saving…" />
<LoadingOverlay active={false} />`}>
      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; width: 100%;">
        <div style="position: relative; min-height: 160px; border: 1px solid var(--color-border-default, #e5e5e5); border-radius: var(--radius-300, 0.5rem); padding: var(--spacing-400, 1rem);">
          <p style="margin: 0;">You can still see this content faintly through the overlay.</p>
          <LoadingOverlay active={true} transparent={true} message="Saving…" />
        </div>
        <div style="position: relative; min-height: 100px; border: 1px solid var(--color-border-default, #e5e5e5); border-radius: var(--radius-300, 0.5rem); padding: var(--spacing-400, 1rem);">
          <p style="margin: 0;">Inactive — the overlay renders nothing.</p>
          <LoadingOverlay active={false} />
        </div>
      </div>
    </Preview>
  </Section>

  <Section id="api" title="API">
    <ApiTable slug="esa-loading-overlay" describe={describe} />
  </Section>

  <Section id="accessibility" title="Accessibility">
    <ul class="a11y">
      <li>The backdrop is a single named graphic — <code>role="img"</code> with <code>message</code> as its accessible name, plus <code>aria-busy</code> — and the visual content inside it is <code>aria-hidden</code> so the name is not read twice. It is <strong>not</strong> a <code>role="status"</code> live region: this page said so until 2026-08-18 and the source had already moved off it, because a region created in the same tick as its text does not announce.</li>
      <li>The backdrop sits at <code>z-index: 10</code> over the parent and intercepts <strong>pointer</strong> interaction while active.</li>
      <li><strong>It does not stop the keyboard, and it cannot.</strong> The overlay is <code>position: absolute</code>, scoped to its nearest positioned ancestor — so a keyboard user can still Tab into controls sitting under an opaque backdrop, and the component cannot make that region <code>inert</code> because it does not own it. Making the covered region inert while loading is the <em>call site's</em> job.</li>
      <li>For long operations, consider moving focus or announcing the busy state at the call site.</li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

</ComponentDoc>
